# API PostHog instrumentation

HTTP route telemetry is **centralized** — do not add per-route `api_request` PostHog capture in handlers.

## Route inventory

- After adding or changing Flask routes, run `make routes-extract` and commit [`Server/endpoints.json`](../../../Server/endpoints.json).
- CI enforces drift via `make routes-extract-verify` in [`.github/workflows/test-callable.yml`](../../../.github/workflows/test-callable.yml).
- After **Test & Coverage** succeeds on `main`, [`.github/workflows/endpoints-sync-posthog.yml`](../../../.github/workflows/endpoints-sync-posthog.yml) POSTs coverage via [`sync_inventory_posthog.py`](../../../Server/scripts/endpoints/sync_inventory_posthog.py): `endpoint_inventory_sync` (full inventory + `dead_endpoints` summary) and one `endpoint_dead_route` event per route with zero `api_request` hits in 7d (reads committed `endpoints.json` only — no `DATABASE_URL`; secrets `POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN` + `POSTHOG_QUERY_API_KEY`).

## `api_request` event contract

Captured in [`Server/app/http/api_telemetry.py`](../../../Server/app/http/api_telemetry.py) + [`posthog_events.py`](../../../Server/app/services/analytics/posthog_events.py).

| Property | Required | Notes |
| -------- | -------- | ----- |
| `endpoint` | yes | `"METHOD /path/{param}"` — use [`normalize_flask_route_rule`](../../../Server/app/utils/http/route_pattern.py) |
| `method` | yes | HTTP verb |
| `status_code` | yes | int |
| `is_error` | yes | `status_code >= 400` (legacy; do not use alone for SLO red/green) |
| `is_server_error` | yes | `status_code >= 500` |
| `error_kind` | yes | `none`, `server`, `auth`, `forbidden`, `not_found`, `rate_limited`, `client` — see [`api_request_error_semantics.py`](../../../Server/app/services/analytics/api_request_error_semantics.py) |
| `expected_client_error` | yes | `true` when the outcome is normal product flow (expired session, role gate, etc.) |
| `duration_ms` | yes | `time.perf_counter()` delta from `g._request_start_perf` in `before_request` |
| `latency_ms` | deprecated | Same value as `duration_ms`; remove after dashboard migration |

Timing starts in [`flask_runtime_routes.py`](../../../Server/app/http/flask_runtime_routes.py) `before_request`. Use `after_request` + `teardown_request` (unhandled exceptions) with `g._api_telemetry_captured` dedupe.

## Intentionally excluded (document if adding similar routes)

- `/healthz`, `/readyz`, `/livez` — probes
- `/static/`, `/assets/` — static delivery
- `OPTIONS` preflight
- SPA `catch_all` (`/login`, etc.)
- `text/event-stream` (SSE) responses
- Unmatched 404s (`request.endpoint is None`)

Rev-share redirect `GET /r/{link_id}` **is** instrumented.

## Examples

```python
# ✅ CORRECT: add route; regenerate inventory
@rev_share_redirect_bp.route("/r/<link_id>", methods=["GET"])
def rev_share_redirect(link_id: str):
    ...

# Then: make routes-extract && commit Server/endpoints.json

# ❌ WRONG: per-route PostHog capture for HTTP telemetry
def my_handler():
    capture_product_event(..., event="api_request", ...)  # use centralized hook instead
```

```python
# ✅ CORRECT: endpoint string format matches inventory
normalize_flask_route_rule("/api/v1/users/<int:user_id>")  # -> "/api/v1/users/{user_id}"
# PostHog endpoint: "GET /api/v1/users/{user_id}"
```
